# Generation provider for POST /api/generate-section and POST /api/funnel-analyze.
# Set either one; if both
# are set, Groq wins because it is free and fast. Force the other with
# GENERATION_PROVIDER=anthropic. With neither, the route returns 503 and the
# builder falls back to copying the master prompt, which still works.

# Free tier. Default. Capped at ~8,000 tokens/minute (measured), so a
# multi-section funnel will hit rate limits — the app waits them out and retries
# automatically. Note Groq counts a request's max_tokens against that budget up
# front, which is why each caller sets its own output ceiling.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional, paid, better output. If you use this, set a HARD MONTHLY BUDGET CAP
# in the Anthropic console: the app is public and has no accounts, so there is
# no reliable per-user limit and that cap is the real backstop.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: "groq" or "anthropic". Overrides the default preference above.
GENERATION_PROVIDER=

# Optional: "groq" or "anthropic", for POST /api/funnel-analyze only. Overrides
# GENERATION_PROVIDER for that route, so you can pay for big-paste analysis
# while keeping HTML generation on the free tier.
#
# Why you would: the analyzer's limit is how much page it can accept, and that
# is set by the per-minute token budget. The fixed part of the request is ~4,350
# tokens (mostly the 110-variation catalogue) plus a 1,200-token reply, so
# Groq's free 8,000/min leaves room for ~9,000 characters of pasted page.
# Anthropic's budget allows ~90,000.
#
# Why NOT to point generation at Anthropic too: it writes the better page, but
# was measured at 34-43s for FAQ-class sections and truncated intermittently
# against the 60s function ceiling.
ANALYZE_PROVIDER=
